    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.13,
      "end_seconds": 64.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "um, a seven out of ten, I suppose"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.23,
      "end_seconds": 70.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "I follow. A few quick ones: fever, fall or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.47,
      "end_seconds": 74.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "no I'd have said so so"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.28,
      "end_seconds": 79.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.62,
      "end_seconds": 86.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.66,
      "text": "actually, uh, my heart's been fine, as far as I know"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.07,
      "end_seconds": 99.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.99,
      "end_seconds": 103.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "no, um, not that I know of"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.08,
      "end_seconds": 119.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Alright, is there someone at home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.78,
      "end_seconds": 126.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "My husband and I live above the shop"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 127.04,
      "end_seconds": 129.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.14,
      "end_seconds": 135.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.26,
      "end_seconds": 139.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.49,
      "end_seconds": 144.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.06,
      "end_seconds": 151.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.26,
      "text": "what's on your current medicine list? I'll explain everything as we go along"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.17,
      "end_seconds": 157.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Eltroxin i take it 100 micrograms, every morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.89,
      "end_seconds": 161.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "okay when did you start it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.02,
      "end_seconds": 165.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "about about a year"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.73,
      "end_seconds": 173.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.15,
      "end_seconds": 178.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "hmm, I've had an underactive thyroid, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.6,
      "end_seconds": 187.11,
      "duration_seconds": 8.51,
      "text": "mm-hmm. Okay I can see an underactive thyroid in your file as well. Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.48,
      "end_seconds": 191.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "my father has Parkinson's disease"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.01,
      "end_seconds": 194.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.57,
      "end_seconds": 203.08,
      "duration_seconds": 7.51,
      "text": "let me think, I had a a caesarean for my second baby nine years ago"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.03,
      "end_seconds": 208.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.74,
      "end_seconds": 211.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.77,
      "end_seconds": 226.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "you are dehydrated and drowsy with a slow odd rhythm on the monitor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.84,
      "end_seconds": 230.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "Please sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.38,
      "end_seconds": 249.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "so where does that leave us? My working impression is a high calcium emergency"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.87,
      "end_seconds": 253.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.07,
      "end_seconds": 270.4,
      "duration_seconds": 16.33,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency it looks like a high calcium emergency but I'd like to confirm. An ECG is what I'd like next for hypercalcaemia it's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.49,
      "end_seconds": 273.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "That makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.28,
      "end_seconds": 285.04,
      "duration_seconds": 10.76,
      "text": "We'll begin with sodium chloride 0.9% 1 litre over one hour single dose. That should help with dehydration. You need hospital fluids and treatment now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.61,
      "end_seconds": 292.58,
      "duration_seconds": 6.97,
      "text": "mm-hmm let's review you straight away before we finish can you repeat the plan back to me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.44,
      "end_seconds": 302.86,
      "duration_seconds": 9.42,
      "text": "So I take the sodium chloride 0.9% 1 litre over one hour and come back straight away. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.76,
      "end_seconds": 309.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "yes, exactly right i think we're done unless you have questions"
    },
